* BEGIN MODEL INA326
* PINOUT R1 IN- IN+ V- R2 VO V+ R1
* PINOUT  1  2   3   4  5  6 7   8
* BEGIN FEATURES
* GAIN AND PHASE
* SLEW RATE
* OUTPUT SWING
* OUTPUT CURRENT THRU THE SUPPLY RAILS
* OUTPUT CURRENT LIMIT
* OUTPUT IMPEDANCE
* CMRR W FREQUENCY EFFECTS
* PSRR W FREQUENCY EFFECTS
* INPUT CAPACITANCE
* INPUT VOLTAGE NOISE THAT VARIES
*   W GAIN AND R1 AND R2 VALUES
* INPUT CURRENT NOISE
* INPUT COMMON MODE VOLTAGE RANGE
* PROPER SWING LIMITS ON THE R2 NODE
* INTERNALY GENERATED RIPPLE THAT
*   VARIES W GAIN AND R1 AND R2 VALUES
* IQ INCL CHANGE W VCC AND TEMPERATURE
* INPUT BIAS CURRENT
* INPUT AND OUTPUT CLAMP DIODES
* TEMP RANGE -40 TO +85 DEG C
*   NOTE THAT THE MODEL IS FUNCTIONAL
*   OVER THIS RANGE BUT NOT ALL
*   PARAMETERS TRACK THE REAL PART
* END FEATURES
*
* BEGIN NOTES
* BECAUSE THIS MODEL HAS A LARGE NUMBER OF
* COMPONENTS AND NODES, YOU WILL SOMETIMES
* HAVE TO ADJUST THE ANALYSIS OPTIONS FOR
* GOOD PERFORMANCE. SOME TYPICAL VALUES
* WOULD BE ITL1=4000 ITL2=1000 ITL4=100 
* BECAUSE THE MODEL DUPLICATES THE INTERNALY
* GENERATED RIPPLE COMPONENTS AT 90,180,AND
* 360 KHZ IT IS IMPORTANT TO WATCH THE SPICE
* SAMPLING RATE IN THE TIME DOMAIN AND SOME-
* TIMES TO SET TSTEP MAX. IF YOU WILL BE
* VIEWING THE RIPPLE THESE PRECAUTIONS
* WILL ALSO HELP PREVENT ALIASING. FURTHER,
* MAKE SURE THE OPTION NUMDGT IS AT LEAST 5
* AS THE RIPPLE IS OFTEN VERY SMALL. A GOOD
* TEST IS TO RUN A SIMULATION WITH THE
* AMPLIFIER INPUT UNCHANGING AND STUDY THE
* OUTPUT AFTER FILTER SETTLING AND MAKE SURE
* IT IS NOT WANDERING. IF IT IS YOU WILL
* NEED TO ADJUST TSTEP MAX. THE RIPPLE
* GENERATORS SLOW THE RUN TIME FOR TIME
* DOMAIN SIMULATIONS WITH 1 TO 3 MINUTES
* BEING TYPICAL.
* END NOTES
*
